{"id": "EUVD-2026-97011", "enisaUuid": "569f6e2d-06b7-3a59-a46a-2fcdea9c06dd", "description": "BotSharp through 5.2.0 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to forge bearer tokens using the hard-coded Jwt:Key in WebStarter appsettings.json. Attackers can sign tokens with the committed HMAC secret and fixed botsharp issuer and audience to impersonate any known user, including administrators, on Authorize-protected API routes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T13:26:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:47:26", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/scisharp-botsharp-public-jwt-signing-key", "https://github.com/SciSharp/BotSharp/blob/a11ee0317cab5c619df1cb5d0c4fc39d1b6e30b4/src/WebStarter/appsettings.json#L16-L20", "https://github.com/SciSharp/BotSharp/blob/a11ee0317cab5c619df1cb5d0c4fc39d1b6e30b4/src/Infrastructure/BotSharp.OpenAPI/BotSharpOpenApiExtensions.cs#L46-L57", "https://github.com/SciSharp/BotSharp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/botsharp-through-5.2.0-authentication-bypass-via-hard-coded-jwt-signing-key"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w9f8-hvcg-hgcm", "CVE-2026-108860"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19466983-950a-32ab-a539-6ad8a494bfac", "product": {"name": "BotSharp", "vendor": {"name": "SciSharp"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22645.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ddc9f026-8de4-3b06-bb6a-af59faed85db", "vendor": {"name": "SciSharp"}}], "isExploited": false}